2,1,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
3,1,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
4,1,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Minato,,Hello everyone. I'm happy to be here. I wonder if we should make sure the plan is something that can actually be finished on time without any big surprises during the digging?,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,May,,"@Minato, timeliness is great, but let's not forget the ""after"" party. I'm more worried about the bills that keep coming once the ribbon is cut. We need a plan that won't bleed the city dry.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is lovely to meet you all. While budgets and schedules are important, I worry that we often focus too much on the beginning. I would like to see if the work truly lasts over time.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Victoria,,"I agree with Shizue. However, durability isn't just about materials; it's about the people. I am concerned about who will actually manage the daily upkeep once the project is complete. We must consider the operational capacity.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,You're all focusing on the ledger and the clock. Let's not forget the ground itself. A plan that looks pretty on a slide but ignores how people actually cross the park is just a fantasy.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, that's a good point. I like the idea of thinking about how people use the park. But if the ground is tricky, it might change how we build the paths, right?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,May,,Exactly. But let's be real: fancy paths are just future liabilities if they're too expensive to scrub or repair. I want to see where the money actually goes for maintenance every year.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, you are quite right to be cautious. However, I believe the best way to predict future costs is to look at how our previous projects have aged. A beautiful drawing can hide many flaws.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, I agree. Past performance is a reliable indicator. I also wonder if we are relying too heavily on a shrinking pool of staff. We need to know who is actually available for the work.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, relying on a ""pool"" is exactly the problem. I'm more interested in the physical reality—where the water pools in August and where the grass is worn down to dirt by actual foot traffic.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Minato,,"I see. So we have to think about the money, the people, and the ground. I'm still a bit worried about the digging part. Do you think the local companies can handle the work without delays?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, local firms are fine, but I'm more interested in the long-term drain on our wallet. If we pick a high-maintenance design, it doesn't matter who digs the hole; we'll be paying for it forever.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Shizue,,"@May, your concern for the city's wallet is very kind. I simply feel that if we see where previous works have failed, we can avoid those same expensive mistakes in the future.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, that is a logical approach. I believe we must also clarify the current balance between professional staff and volunteers to ensure the chosen plan doesn't exceed our actual human capacity for maintenance.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, volunteers are a lovely sentiment, but they aren't a drainage system. I'm less interested in who is ""available"" and more in how the site actually behaves when it rains or when crowds hit.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Minato,,I think I understand now. Everyone has different things they are worried about. I will look into the local firms and the depot notes to see if the construction will be okay.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,May,,I'll be looking into the upkeep ledger spend per hectare and the groundskeeping roll and bought-in services. I need to know exactly what we're paying for and who's actually doing the work.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Shizue,,I shall look into the condition of works from the earlier programme and the record of the eastern avenue planting. I hope to see what has truly stood the test of time.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Victoria,,"I will look into the groundskeeping roll and bought-in services, as well as the volunteer groups working with the division. I need to understand the actual human resources available for the park's daily operation.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll take the timed counts of weekday crossings and the drainage callouts and August heat readings. Let's see if the plans match the actual behavior of the water and the people.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
25,1,,action,Minato,,Regional firms tendering for earth-moving; Depot phasing notes on hoarding the site,"{""action"":""investigate"",""cards"":[""card_03"",""card_04""],""parse"":""ok""}"
